Rules:
  [T1] Use Fastify for high performance, Express for simplicity.
  [T2] Use `async/await` instead of callbacks.
  [T3] Implement centralized error handling middleware.
  [T4] Use Zod for runtime validation.
  [T5] Use Prisma for database access.
  [T6] Implement structured logging (Pino/Winston).
  [T7] Use environment variables with schema validation.
  [T8] Implement graceful shutdown with signal handlers.

Pros:
  - Full-stack JavaScript
  - Large npm ecosystem
  - Fast development

Cons:
  - Single-threaded
  - Memory management
  - Callback pitfalls

Alternatives:
  - Go (performance)
  - Python (simplicity)
  - Java (enterprise)

State: +

